<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! Sealed-store step 3 ~ the document store's rest

!! Contents

* [[Ground and crew|#/ground]] · [[Commit walk|#/walk]] · [[Witness and red window|#/witness]] · [[Collision sheet|#/collisions]] · [[Done when|#/done]] · [[Rulings|#/rulings]].

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/ground`>>

!! Ground and crew

Start the live storage cut after O1 supplies a production verified face, signer and scoped view. One store lead owns sealing, hydration and the document-store callback. A reviewer checks ciphertext addresses, manifest parents, key versions and wrong-face refusals. Step 1 fixes the private-byte format. Step 2 seats the content-key holder and its lockboxes. `content-key-holder.ts` already carries the `freshBase` port and refuses a from-now admission when no base stands; step 3 wires the production callback.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/walk`>>

!! Commit walk

# ''PURE: value and lineage vectors.'' Fix sealed `change` and `checkpoint` references under the step-1 format. Include parent manifests, a random authenticated ciphertext address, a key version and a fresh checkpoint before any new-version change. A bad tag yields no bytes. A second plaintext with equal content still takes a fresh private ciphertext address.
# ''PURE: face decision.'' Define the session-face check over every fetch, write, catalog resolution and content read. A correct key alone grants no read. A refused catalog ask reveals no name. A value the store cannot open reads as a named refusal, never as an absent value.
# ''LIVE: sealed Repo rest.'' Connect the holder's values and lockboxes to the production document store. Seal each stored value, hydrate only after authentication and the face check, and hand the sealed-store shore to the session view. Supply `freshBase` from the document store; commit the checkpoint before the admission's first change or lockbox permits that version.
# ''LIVE: roll and restart.'' Roll content keys at a counted seat removal, retain causal parent references and reopen sealed values after restart. Each replacement takes its re-seal record, signed by the face session that writes it and naming the removal act that authorized the roll (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/rulings`>>).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/witness`>>

!! Witness and red window

Face-checked hydration takes a behavioural witness at the production reader, never a declared red that pins an export name: fetch a sealed change and resolve its catalog name under the authorized session face, then repeat under another verified face holding the same content key and expect both requests to refuse without bytes or a name. Unskip `FRESH_BASE_PRECEDES_FROM_NOW_CHANGE` when the node supplies and exercises its callback. Use a valid key with the wrong face: neither change nor catalog name returns. Then prove authenticated hydration, a fresh base before the first from-now change, and restart from sealed values. The holder's existing port refusal supplies the control; the document store supplies the missing witness.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/collisions`>>

!! Collision sheet

| Seam | Step-3 hand-off |
|---|---|
| N and W | Consume the final AID, sealed identities and production session signer; leave inception and `session-signer.ts` with their owners. |
| O1 | Consume the verified face and scoped view after its live mount. O1 keeps the working-address bytes and session switch. |
| S8 | Leave the selves plane and `sealed-acts.ts` with S8. Share the custody shore through its typed ports. |
| H | Hosting HOT rows and serving rows follow their own custody classes. Step 3 seals Repo document values. |
| X | X reads sealed restart and wrong-face refusal through the node; its driver changes no store format. |

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/done`>>

!! Done when

Repo values rest under randomized authenticated sealing. Every document and content door checks the session face. A wrong face learns no change or catalog name, even with the key. A from-now admission starts at a fresh checkpoint; a restart hydrates authenticated values and refuses tampering.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/rulings`>>

!! Rulings

The roadmap's sealed-store ruling and step-3 pointer hold this cut (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/rulings`>>; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/side-lanes`>>). The re-seal proof stands ruled: its record's format lands with this step.

<<~/ahu>>

